              fixedCode: "#include <iostream>\n#include <mutex>\nstd::mutex m;\nvoid work() {\n  std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(m);\n  std::cout << \"working\\n\";\n}\nint main() { work(); }",
              explanation: "Calling lock() manually and returning early skips unlock(), leaving the mutex locked forever. std::lock_guard releases the lock in its destructor on every exit path, including early returns."
